  "worked_solution": "First, we add the columns for $\u00acP$ and $\u00acQ,$ \nwhere the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the columns for $P$ and $Q,$ respectively.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,\u00acQ\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $\u00acP\u2228\u00acQ.$ Remember that $\u00acP\u2228\u00acQ$ is true if either $\u00acP$ is true or $\u00acQ$ is true.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,\u00acQ\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\u2228\u00acQ\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
